From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alphi <alphi@starchaser.local>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 13:49:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(core): clamp te_width to 0..32767 in canvas_f, and never
 report a negative width from rtext_charwidth

The "#X f <n>" line of a patch file reaches canvas_f, which stored atom_getfloatarg(0) into the signed short te_width
unchecked. "f -3" (or "f 40000", which wraps) left a negative width. rtext_formattext (g_rtext.c) takes
widthlimit_c = rtext_charwidth(x) as the line length: a negative value makes maxindex_c and maxindex_b negative and the
strncpy that copies the line gets a negative (huge) length: heap overrun, "malloc(): corrupted top size", about 11 s
after the patch opened (the host leak review's patch ab-ctl-comment-loop.pd). The atom path (g_text.c) already clamps
its width.

canvas_f: negative or NaN -> 0 (auto width), above SHRT_MAX -> 32767. rtext_charwidth: a negative te_width (set by any
other writer) reads as 0. Valid widths (0..32767) are unchanged.

Depended on by: the fork's CommentObject / TextObject width handling and every patch with a "f" line on a text, comment
or object box. Drop it only when upstream Pd clamps te_width in canvas_f itself.
---
 src/g_canvas.c | 6 +++++-
 src/g_rtext.c  | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/g_canvas.c b/src/g_canvas.c
index 56ebeb6..0a14535 100644
--- a/src/g_canvas.c
+++ b/src/g_canvas.c
@@ -2076,7 +2076,11 @@ static void canvas_f(t_canvas *x, t_symbol *s, int argc, t_atom *argv)
         ;
     if ((ob = pd_checkobject(&g->g_pd)))
     {
-        ob->te_width = atom_getfloatarg(0, argc, argv);
+            /* te_width is a signed short: "f -3" or "f 40000" in a patch file
+            must not leave it negative (rtext_formattext would then take a
+            negative line length and overrun its buffer). 0 means auto. */
+        t_float width = atom_getfloatarg(0, argc, argv);
+        ob->te_width = (width >= 0 ? (width > 32767 ? 32767 : width) : 0);
         if (glist_isvisible(x))
         {
             gobj_vis(g, x, 0);
diff --git a/src/g_rtext.c b/src/g_rtext.c
index 3730941..21ce0d2 100644
--- a/src/g_rtext.c
+++ b/src/g_rtext.c
@@ -203,7 +203,7 @@ static void rtext_findscreenlocation(t_rtext *x)
 int rtext_charwidth(t_rtext *x)
 {
     if (x->x_text)
-        return (x->x_text->te_width);
+        return (x->x_text->te_width < 0 ? 0 : x->x_text->te_width);
     else return (0); /* LATER do we want a width field for drawtext obj? */
 }
 
